Description: Specify a wide class of linear and generalized linear mixed models using familiar 'ASReml' or 'brms'-style
    formula syntax, and estimate them via 'INLA' or 'brms' ('Stan'). Returns
    results in formats compatible with the standard R modelling ecosystem
    including 'summary()', 'emmeans' and 'marginaleffects'. The package supports a range of responses from the exponential family (and a few beyond this), along with a few random effects 
    covariance/residual structures including genotype-by-environment variances, per-level residual variances, and known-covariance genomic and
    pedigree matrices among others.
